{"version":1,"createdAt":"2026-08-28T22:19:38.832Z","chunks":[{"id":"account.md#0","docId":"account.md","title":"Account and payment","section":"Account and payment > Payment methods","text":"We accept Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Apple Pay, Google Pay and PayPal.\nSubscriptions can use any card, Apple Pay or PayPal. Bank transfer is available\nfor wholesale accounts only."},{"id":"account.md#1","docId":"account.md","title":"Account and payment","section":"Account and payment > Updating a card","text":"Change the card from the account page under Payment. If a subscription payment\nfails we retry twice over four days and email you each time before the box is\ncancelled."},{"id":"account.md#2","docId":"account.md","title":"Account and payment","section":"Account and payment > Changing your delivery address","text":"Update it from the account page before the roast day. Changes made after the box\nis roasted cannot be applied, because the label is already printed."},{"id":"account.md#3","docId":"account.md","title":"Account and payment","section":"Account and payment > Deleting your account and data","text":"Ask us to delete your account and we do it within 30 days, including order\nhistory. Anything we are legally required to keep for tax purposes is retained\nin accounting records only. We never sell customer data and never share it with\nadvertisers."},{"id":"account.md#4","docId":"account.md","title":"Account and payment","section":"Account and payment > Trouble signing in","text":"Sign-in uses a one-time link sent by email rather than a password, so there is\nnothing to reset. If the link does not arrive, check spam and confirm you are\nusing the address the order was placed with."},{"id":"coffee.md#0","docId":"coffee.md","title":"Coffee, grind and storage","section":"Coffee, grind and storage > Choosing a grind","text":"We grind to order. Choose whole bean if you own a grinder, because coffee stales\nseveral times faster once ground.\n\n- Espresso: fine, like table salt\n- Moka pot and Aeropress: medium-fine\n- Pour over, V60 and Chemex: medium\n- Cafetiere and French press: coarse, like raw sugar\n- Cold brew: extra coarse"},{"id":"coffee.md#1","docId":"coffee.md","title":"Coffee, grind and storage","section":"Coffee, grind and storage > How long the coffee stays good","text":"Beans are at their best between 5 and 21 days after the roast date printed on\nthe bag. They are perfectly drinkable for about three months. Ground coffee\nshould be used within two weeks."},{"id":"coffee.md#2","docId":"coffee.md","title":"Coffee, grind and storage","section":"Coffee, grind and storage > Storing it properly","text":"Keep the bag sealed, at room temperature, away from light. The valve on the bag\nlets carbon dioxide out without letting oxygen in, so the original bag is better\nthan most containers. Do not refrigerate: coffee absorbs smells and condensation\nruins it. Freezing works only for unopened bags you will not touch for months."},{"id":"coffee.md#3","docId":"coffee.md","title":"Coffee, grind and storage","section":"Coffee, grind and storage > Decaf","text":"Our decaf is Swiss Water processed, which uses no chemical solvents. It is\nroasted on the same days as everything else and ships with the same guarantee."},{"id":"coffee.md#4","docId":"coffee.md","title":"Coffee, grind and storage","section":"Coffee, grind and storage > Allergens","text":"Coffee is roasted in a facility that handles no nuts, dairy or gluten. Flavoured\ncoffees are not something we sell."},{"id":"returns.md#0","docId":"returns.md","title":"Returns and refunds","section":"Returns and refunds > The freshness guarantee","text":"If you do not like the coffee, tell us within 30 days of delivery and we will\nrefund the order in full. You do not need to send the beans back, and you do not\nneed a reason. We would rather lose the sale than have you drink coffee you do\nnot enjoy."},{"id":"returns.md#1","docId":"returns.md","title":"Returns and refunds","section":"Returns and refunds > How to start a refund","text":"Reply to your order confirmation email with the word \"refund\", or use the\ncontact form with your order number. Refunds are approved by a person, usually\nwithin one working day, and land back on the original payment method in three to\nfive working days."},{"id":"returns.md#2","docId":"returns.md","title":"Returns and refunds","section":"Returns and refunds > What is not covered","text":"Wholesale orders over 5kg are final sale, because they are roasted to order in\nquantities we cannot resell. Gift cards are non-refundable but never expire.\nEquipment such as grinders and brewers can be returned unused within 14 days."},{"id":"returns.md#3","docId":"returns.md","title":"Returns and refunds","section":"Returns and refunds > Damaged or wrong items","text":"Send a photo of the bag and the packaging. We ship a replacement the same roast\nday and do not ask for the original back."},{"id":"shipping.md#0","docId":"shipping.md","title":"Shipping and delivery","section":"Shipping and delivery > When your order ships","text":"Roasting happens Monday, Wednesday and Friday morning. Orders placed before 6am\non a roast day ship the same afternoon; anything later goes out on the next\nroast day. We do this so beans reach you within 48 hours of roasting rather than\nsitting in a warehouse."},{"id":"shipping.md#1","docId":"shipping.md","title":"Shipping and delivery","section":"Shipping and delivery > Delivery times","text":"| Destination | Carrier | Typical time |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| United Kingdom | Royal Mail Tracked 24 | 1 to 2 working days |\n| Ireland and EU | An Post / DPD | 3 to 5 working days |\n| United States | DHL Express | 4 to 7 working days |\n| Rest of world | DHL Express | 7 to 14 working days |"},{"id":"shipping.md#2","docId":"shipping.md","title":"Shipping and delivery","section":"Shipping and delivery > Shipping cost","text":"UK delivery is £3.95, and free on orders over £30. EU delivery is £8.50 flat.\nUnited States delivery is £12 flat. Subscriptions always ship free, on every\ndestination, from the first box onward."},{"id":"shipping.md#3","docId":"shipping.md","title":"Shipping and delivery","section":"Shipping and delivery > Tracking","text":"A tracking link is emailed when the parcel is collected, not when the order is\nplaced. If the tracking has not moved after two working days, contact us and we\nwill open a case with the carrier."},{"id":"shipping.md#4","docId":"shipping.md","title":"Shipping and delivery","section":"Shipping and delivery > Customs and duties","text":"Orders outside the UK may attract import duty. We declare the true value on the\ncustoms form and cannot mark parcels as gifts. Duty is paid by the recipient."},{"id":"subscriptions.md#0","docId":"subscriptions.md","title":"Subscriptions","section":"Subscriptions > How the subscription works","text":"Choose a bag size and a frequency, and we roast and ship on that cadence. The\ncard is charged the morning of the roast day, not on signup, so you always know\nwhat is coming before you pay for it."},{"id":"subscriptions.md#1","docId":"subscriptions.md","title":"Subscriptions","section":"Subscriptions > Changing frequency","text":"Available frequencies are weekly, fortnightly, every three weeks, and monthly.\nChange it from the account page under Subscriptions, or reply to any dispatch\nemail. The change applies to the next box, not the one already roasting."},{"id":"subscriptions.md#2","docId":"subscriptions.md","title":"Subscriptions","section":"Subscriptions > Pausing and skipping","text":"Skip a single box from the account page up to 24 hours before the roast day.\nPausing stops all future boxes indefinitely and keeps your settings; there is no\nminimum term and no cancellation fee. Resuming picks up the same schedule."},{"id":"subscriptions.md#3","docId":"subscriptions.md","title":"Subscriptions","section":"Subscriptions > Cancelling","text":"Cancel from the account page under Subscriptions, or reply to any email from us\nasking to cancel. It takes effect immediately unless a box has already been\nroasted, in which case that final box ships and nothing further is charged."},{"id":"subscriptions.md#4","docId":"subscriptions.md","title":"Subscriptions","section":"Subscriptions > Subscriber pricing","text":"Subscribers pay 15% less than the one-off price and always ship free. The\ndiscount applies automatically and stacks with nothing else."},{"id":"wholesale.md#0","docId":"wholesale.md","title":"Wholesale and offices","section":"Wholesale and offices > Who wholesale is for","text":"Cafes, restaurants, offices and anyone using more than 5kg a month. Pricing\nstarts at £16 per kilogram and drops at 20kg and 50kg per month."},{"id":"wholesale.md#1","docId":"wholesale.md","title":"Wholesale and offices","section":"Wholesale and offices > Getting started","text":"Email wholesale with your location, the equipment you brew on, and roughly how\nmuch coffee you go through in a week. We send samples of three roasts free of\ncharge, and a dialling-in visit is included for accounts within the M25."},{"id":"wholesale.md#2","docId":"wholesale.md","title":"Wholesale and offices","section":"Wholesale and offices > Wholesale terms","text":"Accounts are invoiced monthly on 30-day terms after the first three orders,\nwhich are paid up front. Wholesale orders are roasted to order and are not\nrefundable, though we will replace anything that arrives damaged or stale."},{"id":"wholesale.md#3","docId":"wholesale.md","title":"Wholesale and offices","section":"Wholesale and offices > Office coffee","text":"Offices under 5kg a month are better served by a large subscription, which is\ncheaper per bag and needs no account setup. We can invoice a company rather than\ncharging a card if that is easier for your finance team."}],"keyword":{"postings":{"12":[16,1],"14":[12,1,15,1],"15":[23,1],"16":[24,1],"21":[6,1],"24":[15,1,21,1],"30":[3,1,10,1,16,1,26,1],"48":[14,1],"50":[16,